Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below are the columns you will really use and why

• bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips  
  – starttime / stoptime: to derive the calendar day of the ride (DATE(starttime))  
  – tripduration (optional): not needed but can help in QC  
  – start_station_id etc.: not needed for the requested metric, but present  
  Condition: EXTRACT(YEAR FROM starttime) = 2016  

• bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_stations  
  – id: station identifier (to join with daily tables)  
  – latitude, longitude: to compute distance from NYC (40.7128, ‑74.0060)  
  Condition: ST_DISTANCE(ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude), ST_GEOGPOINT(‑74.0060, 40.7128)) <= 50 000 (metres)  

• bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016  
  – id: station identifier (to keep only the chosen station)  
  – date: calendar day of observation  
  – element: filter to ‘PRCP’ (precipitation)  
  – value: raw precipitation in 0.1 mm; divide by 10 to obtain millimetres  
  – qflag: keep only rows where qflag IS NULL (valid, un‑flagged)  

---------------------------------------------------------------------------  
Ten exploratory → final queries (each limited to 20 rows where applicable)  
---------------------------------------------------------------------------  

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at raw Citi Bike trips
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Distinct years of Citi Bike data (check that 2016 exists)
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM starttime) AS yr
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips`
ORDER BY yr;
```

```sql
-- 3. Number of Citi Bike trips per day in 2016 (sample 20 days)
SELECT
  DATE(starttime) AS ride_day,
  COUNT(*)        AS trips
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM starttime) = 2016
GROUP BY ride_day
ORDER BY ride_day
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. All GHCN stations within 50 km of NYC’s coordinates (preview)
SELECT
  id,
  name,
  latitude,
  longitude,
  ST_DISTANCE(
      ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude),
      ST_GEOGPOINT(-74.0060, 40.7128)
  ) AS distance_m
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_stations`
WHERE ST_DISTANCE(
        ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude),
        ST_GEOGPOINT(-74.0060, 40.7128)
      ) <= 50000   -- 50 km
ORDER BY distance_m
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Pick the single nearest valid station (should return 1 row)
SELECT
  id,
  name,
  latitude,
  longitude,
  ST_DISTANCE(
      ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude),
      ST_GEOGPOINT(-74.0060, 40.7128)
  ) AS distance_m
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_stations`
ORDER BY distance_m
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 6. Raw 2016 precipitation records for that station (replace <STATION_ID>)
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`
WHERE id = '<STATION_ID>'
  AND element = 'PRCP'
  AND qflag IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Daily total precipitation (mm) for the chosen station (sample 20 days)
SELECT
  date,
  SUM(value)/10.0 AS prcp_mm          -- raw value is in 0.1 mm
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`
WHERE id = '<STATION_ID>'
  AND element = 'PRCP'
  AND qflag IS NULL
GROUP BY date
ORDER BY date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Mark each day as rainy (>5 mm) or non‑rainy (sample 20)
WITH daily_prcp AS (
  SELECT
    date,
    SUM(value)/10.0 AS prcp_mm
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`
  WHERE id = '<STATION_ID>'
    AND element = 'PRCP'
    AND qflag IS NULL
  GROUP BY date
)
SELECT
  date,
